the first song I ever wrote I was about  five or six I made it for my mom and I  would sing it to her when I was around  the house and I would ask her mum please  can I keep your dress please keep your  shoes can you please I just wanted to be  a phrase how really I always start with  lyrics it's always when something  significant happens I take it I write it  down and when I go into the studio I  then put the words to melody and if I  still feel the same way about the the  words that I've written that I feel like  I should definitely carry on with the  story everything I write about is is  quite personal and it's all very much  biographical so I'm more inspired by  words than by melodies and then I'd like  to call my music dance crying because  they're all quite sad stories in a way  but then with the production I want it  to be more pop and I want it to be  something that people can dance to I  guess my writing process is kind of  crazy I write so many songs and out of  ten I like one oh I wish every homesick  is well a feeling and it was one that I  was definitely feeling towards the end  of writing the album when I spend so  much time on the road and I spend so  much time away from home and I'm  traveling so much it's really when I'm  in a hot place like LA and it starts  raining that I miss London the most and  it's you know you spend so much time  away and it's like the the things that  you hate about home and the ones that  you miss the most so the bad weather was  definitely I guess that the main  influence behind everything and singing  about that the reason you know you make  all these little sacrifices is to kind  of make your dreams come true and you  work pretty hard because this is  something that you've you've always  wanted but there's no denying that you  occasionally get home second you do miss  that  with all the features that I've done  I've always wanted to work with people  that did something quite different to  what I do so when I do come together  with them it's it's still quite distinct  what I'm able to bring to the table I  was really lucky I got to work and write  it with Chris Martin and I was in London  prior to going to to LA to write and I  was in a meeting and somebody had asked  me who I would love to work with and I  said oh I would love to get in the  studio with Chris Martin it was more  just me just putting it out there into  the world and I didn't expect for for  one of the lovely women who were in the  meeting and she said oh I work really  closely with Coldplay why didn't he send  me some of the songs from your album and  I can send him to Chris he's very busy  but we can see maybe make something work  and I was like okay cool so I chose a  few songs on the album and I sent them  over and I just get an email going why  didn't you go down to the studio and go  meet Chris and play him some stuff and I  was like okay cool I don't really think  anything was going to come of it  and so I went to the studio and just sat  there me Chris and his engineer Bill and  we just listened to all the songs in the  album and what I was nervous just kind  of playing all the songs it was also  really interesting to kind of get  feedback from someone who I guess in a  way makes popular music but it's so  different to the kind of music that I  make and just to hear hear their opinion  especially as an artist that I  appreciate and admire and he listened to  everything and he was like great why  don't we just try and write something  else but for the album and I was like  right now he was like yeah let's do it  and he just sat on the piano and it was  kind of crazy hearing Chris play play  the keys because the second he start  playing I was like arthas's there's  Coldplay someone who'd been hearing on  the radio I guess your whole life  playing less than a meter away from  mirrors is really surreal  I I had a session the next day so why I  left and we kind of left her that he  would write some of it and I would write  some of it and we could come back  together and put our ideas but when I  left I also thought I was never going to  come back so I was kind of mentally  prepared to just write it on my own and  so I just dropped him a text and I was  like okay I have this idea and I have  this time free I know you're busy maybe  you could we could get back in together  he's like yeah come down on on Wednesday  and let's finish the song and we wrote  the whole song Chris started playing  some chords on the piano and we just  went from there we had mics set up in  the room and I was just humming melodies  and trying to see what sounds good and  we were making up different parts and I  guess some of it sounded like words some  of it was just mumbling but it was it's  probably the first time I'd ever I'd  ever done a song based on melody to  begin where they knew what the concept  was going to be of it seeing as you know  we'd already come up with a title for  home second I knew what I was gonna  write about that it was the first time  that I just kind of went on the basis of  melody and it was really what kind of  drove the song oh and I went in and I  recorded it and then I I kind I just  went please because will you sing on it  because the whole time when we were  writing it we were singing it together  and it just felt so weird when I went  into the to the booth and sang it on my  own and he agreed to do it and that's  really how it how it came about maybe it  was probably the last song to finish off  the album it was really that last trip  to LA that I made where when I hopped on  the plane back to London I was like okay  I feel like I'm done with the album  so this elements all been just very  personal I feel like I've had a lot to  say just just because I never had the  opportunity to really just put it down  and try and tell a story and and you  know kind of create a project like that  like an album and be able to allow the  fans and listeners to really get to know  me on a more personal level so I think I  really just had the opportunity to  travel and I learned to be more open and  learn to not be so afraid of my own  thoughts and speak up about just things  that I felt were really personal to me  especially when I would walk in a room  with producers and songwriters that I'd  never worked with before it really  taught me to be more confident and just  go out there and just really say what I  felt and not and not be embarrassed and  not be afraid of it and I guess I just  learned that that the only person that  was gonna get a real on a song out for  me was me but that's when I feel like I  found clarity and I was really able to  just write but I tend to write quite  quickly but this this one just felt  really easy I guess it was it was just  the perfect closing song  [Music]
 

